Z||000000||KRMFiero||07-30-2001||11:08 PM||||I picked up a Spoiler today, i belive it is a stock one, looks it anyway. So Where do I drill the holes on my decklid? how far from side/from back... also on the passanger side the mounting bolt is in a different location then the driverside, it apprears that the bolt could be put into another spot like a inch closer to the other one, anyone know what im talking about? can i move it/ what?<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-30-2001||11:22 PM||||I have a decklid with the spoiler off right now.  I can get the dimensions for the hole locations give them to you tomorrow since I don't have internet access at home.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ronnie||07-30-2001||11:59 PM||||I just installed a factory spoiler on my 88 GT last Sat.The GT spoiler holes are actually further apart,(front to back), than a coupe's holes. You can mount it either way , but the holes are like that for a reason.The studs are 29" apart in width.That put my holes 10" in from each edge of the decklid.<P>------------------<BR>88GT auto,88Formula T-Top,86GT 4spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3fierossign.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||grinthock||07-31-2001||12:02 AM||||On a fastback you don't mount a spoiler, they are only made for NOTCHbacks!<P>(J/K I love fastbacks with no spoiler)<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://grinthock.2y.net/pics/87gt/S_P000386.JPG">   <P>Home page: <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroworld.com</A> Home  of the fiero voting booth!<BR>Owner of 85 GT<BR>87 GT Silver<BR>1995 Ford Escort Wagoon POS||||reg||1
